        a                       ecrm:E12_Production ;
        ecrm:P108_has_produced  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1e1625d0-679a-3a18-adf8-754e4346eefc> ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      "metal & twist: gilt or silver (?) S. Tightness of wrap: medium. Slightly S spun silk filaments. Satin selvedges: purply brown think silk with a little blue thicker silk.\nThe brocade is relatively intact"@en , "the rest of the velvet is voided NOT brocaded."@en , "the gilt thread seemed to have been used mostly in accents: in the serrated leaves at the side, in the cenre of the smallest circles"@en , "4/1 twill, count 23, shots between pile 2"@en , "Woven silk brocade velvet with vertical and horizontal point repeat with 4 minimum pattern areas. Satin foundation styructure 4/1 satin, warp: silk, ivory, regular thickness. Weft: cotton, single strand. Satin & velvet warp order 3-1-2. Velvet structure: green silk, pile counts, warps 11, along weft 13. Binding weft threads: silk, thin and less thin. Brocade structure, part brocaded"@en ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/617> , <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/900> ;
